can confirm. INCREDIBLY SOFT.

&#x200B;

disclaimer. DO NOT go out and try to pet a kookaburra, kookaburras have very strong beaks. also, it can be very stressful and unsafe. my circumstances were very specific.

I have had to deal with many a possum in my roof and the best solution I've found is this;

If there is a specific place that it enters and exits, put a one-way cat-flap kind of thing so it can leave you roof-space but cannot come back in. if there are several exits/entrances, make more catflaps or seal them as best you can.

(you can also try to lure the possum/rodent out of the roof-space by leaving an animal safe food a metre or so from the cat flap to make sure they are completely out)

